cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CAES Atlas: thermodynamic screening of combustion-free compressed-air energy storage"
abstract: >-
  Screening tool for compressed-air energy storage concepts that use neither fuel nor a
  high-temperature thermal store. Ambient-diabatic, low-temperature adiabatic and
  heat-and-power plants are solved as closed charge-discharge cycles on a
  per-kilogram-of-air basis, with real-fluid properties, finite-effectiveness heat
  exchangers, a moisture-safe expansion envelope and a complete exergy balance.
authors:
  - family-names: "D'Acunzio"
    given-names: "Tommaso"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-9081-1852"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tomdacu/caes-atlas"
keywords:
  - compressed-air energy storage
  - CAES
  - energy storage
  - exergy analysis
  - thermodynamics
  - district heating
type: software
